---
import AuditLayout from "@/layouts/AuditLayout.astro";
import AuditLinkReview from "@/components/AuditLinkReview.svelte";
import { ROUTES } from "@/lib/routes";
---

<AuditLayout title="Link review">
  <nav class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
    <a href={ROUTES.audit} class="hover:text-accent">All states</a>
    <span aria-hidden="true"> / </span>
    <span class="text-ink">Link review</span>
  </nav>

  <h1 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-bold text-ink">Unconfirmed cited links</h1>
  <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-muted max-w-3xl">
    The weekly sweep flags every cited URL the checker could not confirm: hosts that reject automated requests (HTTP
    401, 403, 405, or 429), connections that reset or fail TLS negotiation, and server errors (HTTP 5xx). None of these
    establishes that a page is gone — many State Education Agency sites block automated clients while serving the page
    normally in a browser. Open each URL; if it loads, accept it. An accepted URL is recorded at the status it was
    accepted for and re-appears here if that status later changes. A URL that is definitively gone (HTTP 404 or 410) is
    treated as broken instead, and routed to datapoint re-verification.
  </p>

  <AuditLinkReview client:load />
</AuditLayout>
